# ── Never publish ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Obsidian's OWN generated stylesheet, kept locally so tests can check our rules
# against the real app.css. It is not ours to redistribute.
app.css

# THE WHOLE SCRATCH VAULT.
#
# test-vault/ is where the plugin is exercised by hand, and it accumulated real
# notes doing it: a personal daily journal, notes naming colleagues and an
# employer, private goals. It also holds data.json, which carries live calendar
# URLs including private ICS tokens, plus megabytes of cached calendar bodies,
# and a third-party theme that is not ours to redistribute.
#
# Ignoring the folder piecemeal left personal notes in the untracked-but-not-
# ignored state, where a single `git add -A` publishes them permanently. One
# rule, no gaps.
#
# The cost is one test: tests/corpus.test.ts's vault-coverage check skips when
# the folder is absent. Every row's parse/regenerate proof is pure and still
# runs from a clone — see the note in that file.
test-vault/
